# Build context for the serving image.
#
# Without this file the context is 8.6 GB, nearly all of it training data the
# serving path never opens. Docker uploads the whole context before the first
# instruction runs, so an untrimmed build spends minutes shipping files no
# layer will ever copy — and on a hosted builder it is minutes of upload from
# whoever started it.
#
# Stated as plain exclusions rather than an exclude-then-re-include chain:
# .dockerignore negation across nested directories is subtle enough to get
# wrong quietly, and getting it wrong here means an image whose /health says
# status "error" because the checkpoint silently never arrived.

# ─── Training data — 8.5 GB, read only by the notebooks ────────────────
data/

# ─── The one large artefact: the held-out window set (157 MB) ──────────
# Stage 6 measured the reported metrics on it; serving never reads it.
outputs/stage3_windows/

# ─── Figures and intermediate arrays under outputs/ ────────────────────
outputs/**/*.npy
outputs/**/*.png

# What survives is what api/state.py actually loads — best_tstcn.keras,
# scaler.pkl, type_risk_weights.json — plus a few KB of metrics JSON.

# ─── Local environment ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/

# ─── Research material, not serving material ───────────────────────────
notebooks/
reports/
docs/
tests/

# ─── Repo furniture ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git/
.gitignore
.dockerignore
